hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3049","**\nNarrated to us 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-'Ala', narrated to us Sufyan, who said: I heard it from Ibrahim ibn 'Uqbah, who said: I heard Kurayb narrating, on the authority of Ibn 'Abbas (RA), that the Prophet (ﷺ) departed from Makkah. When he reached al-Rawha', a group of riders came towards him, and he greeted them. He asked, \Who are these people?\"" They replied"","" \""The Muslims.\"" He then asked"","" \""Who are you?\"" They said"","" \""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ).\"" A woman among them was startled and lifted her young child from the saddle"","" holding him by his arm. She asked"","" \""O Messenger of Allah"","" does this child have a Hajj?\"" He (ﷺ) replied"","" \""Yes"","" and you will receive its reward.\""\n\nIbrahim (ibn 'Uqbah) said: I narrated this hadith to Ibn al-Munkadir"","" so he performed Hajj with all his family. It was also narrated to us 'Ali ibn Khashram"","" who informed us Sufyan"","" and he did not say"","" \""She was startled"",""\"" but rather said: She asked"","" \""Does this child have a Hajj?\"" He (ﷺ) replied"","" \""Yes"","" and you will receive its reward.\"" In all versions"","" it is narrated from..."""""
